.policy "eslint-no-octal" revision 3
.description "Avoid numeric literals that start with a zero followed by a digit; legacy octal is deprecated and easily misread as decimal."
.language typescript
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// ESLint's no-octal: a number literal whose source starts with 0 and another digit. `071` is the legacy octal
// 57, and `08` a decimal written with a leading zero; both are errors in strict code.
//   var a = 071;   var b = 08;      → reported
//   0o71   0x71   0   0.5   0e1      fine
// No options.
.violation no_octal(at: node) code "no-octal"
    "Write this number with a 0o prefix if it is octal, or drop the leading zero if it is decimal."
    suppress eslint "no-octal"
no_octal(n) :- kind(n, "number"), glob("0[0-9]*", n).
